Ta có
$\lim \frac{3n-1}{1+6n}=\lim \frac{3-\frac{1}{n}}{\frac{1}{n}+6}=\frac{3}{6}=\frac{1}{2}\,\,$vì $\lim \frac{1}{n}=0$;
$\lim \frac{2n+1}{4n-1}=\lim \frac{2+\frac{1}{n}}{4-\frac{1}{n}}=\frac{2}{4}=\frac{1}{2}$ vì $\lim \frac{1}{n}=0$
$\lim \frac{4n+1}{3n-1}=\lim \frac{4+\frac{1}{n}}{3-\frac{1}{n}}=\frac{4}{3}$ vì $\lim \frac{1}{n}=0$;
$\lim \frac{n+1}{2n-1}=\lim \frac{1+\frac{1}{n}}{2-\frac{1}{n}}=\frac{1}{2}$ vì $\lim \frac{1}{n}=0$.
